/-!
# Global generation of invertible modules of large degree on an integral curve

In Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B5D] — a field `k` and a proper one-dimensional `k`-scheme `X` with
`H⁰(X, 𝒪_X) = k` — assume `X` integral of genus `g`, and let `ℒ` be an invertible `𝒪_X`-module.
[Stacks, Tag 0E3C] asserts that `ℒ` is generated by its global sections if `deg(ℒ) ≥ 2g`, and
[Stacks, Tag 0E3D] that moreover `H⁰(X, ℒ) ⟶ H⁰(X, ℒ|_Z)` is surjective for a nonempty
zero-dimensional closed subscheme `Z` with `deg(ℒ) ≥ 2g - 1 + deg(Z)`.

## Main definitions

* `CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.subschemeRestriction`: the restriction `ℒ|_Z = ℒ ⊗ i_* 𝒪_Z` of
  `ℒ` to a closed subscheme `i : Z ⟶ X`, as an `𝒪_X`-module.
* `CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.subschemeRestrictionπ`: the restriction map `ℒ ⟶ ℒ|_Z`.

## Main results

* `CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.finrank_cohomology_zero_le_of_mono`: a coherent submodule of an
  invertible module which has nonzero first cohomology has at most `g` linearly independent global
  sections.
* `CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.genericPoint_notMem_supp_cokernel_globalSectionsHom`: an
  invertible module with a nonzero global section is generated by its global sections at the
  generic point.
* `CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.isGeneratedByGlobalSections_of_two_mul_genus_le`:
  [Stacks, Tag 0E3C].
* `CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.shortExact_idealTwistι_subschemeRestrictionπ`: the sequence
  `0 ⟶ ℐ_Z ℒ ⟶ ℒ ⟶ ℒ|_Z ⟶ 0` is short exact.
* `CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.isGeneratedByGlobalSections_and_surjective_subschemeRestrictionπ`:
  [Stacks, Tag 0E3D].

## The argument

Let `ℒ' ⊆ ℒ` be the submodule generated by the global sections, the kernel of `ℒ ⟶ 𝒬` where `𝒬`
is the cokernel of `AlgebraicGeometry.globalSectionsHom ℒ`; in the source's notation
`ℒ' = ℐℒ` with `ℐ` the ideal of the base locus `Z`, and `𝒬 = ℒ|_Z`. By Riemann-Roch
`dim H⁰(X, ℒ) ≥ deg(ℒ) + 1 - g ≥ g + 1 > 0`, so `ℒ` has a nonzero section, `ℒ'` agrees with `ℒ` at
the generic point, and `𝒬` is supported in dimension zero.

Every global section of `ℒ` lies in `ℒ'`, so `H⁰(X, ℒ') = H⁰(X, ℒ)` and `H⁰(X, ℒ) ⟶ H⁰(X, 𝒬)` is
zero; the long exact sequence then embeds `H⁰(X, 𝒬)` into `H¹(X, ℒ')`. If `𝒬 ≠ 0` then
`H⁰(X, 𝒬) ≠ 0` by [Stacks, Tag 0B3J], so `H¹(X, ℒ') ≠ 0` and clause (5) of [Stacks, Tag 0BS2]
gives a nonzero map `ℒ' ⟶ ω_X`, which is injective (`mono_of_ne_zero_of_mono`). Then
`g + 1 ≤ dim H⁰(X, ℒ') ≤ dim H⁰(X, ω_X) = g` by equation [Stacks, Tag 0BY8], which is absurd. So
`𝒬 = 0`.

The source uses [Stacks, Tag 0E3B] only to know `Z ≠ X`, i.e. that `ℒ` has a nonzero global
section; Riemann-Roch gives this directly.

For [Stacks, Tag 0E3D], `deg(Z) ≥ 1` because `Z` is nonempty, so [Stacks, Tag 0E3C] gives global
generation; and `deg(ℒ) > 2g - 2 + deg(Z)`, so `H¹(X, ℐ_Z ℒ) = 0` by [Stacks, Tag 0E3A] and the
long exact sequence of `0 ⟶ ℐ_Z ℒ ⟶ ℒ ⟶ ℒ|_Z ⟶ 0` gives the surjectivity.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E3C](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E3C)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E3D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E3D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E3A](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E3A)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C6K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C6K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E3B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E3B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BS2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BS2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BS3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BS3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BY8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BY8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B3J](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B3J)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open Stacks.ModuleStalk

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

namespace CohenMacaulayCurveSituation

variable {S : CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.{u}}

/-- **A coherent submodule of an invertible module with nonvanishing first cohomology has at most
`g` independent global sections**, on an integral `X` in Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B5D]. Clause (5)
of [Stacks, Tag 0BS2] gives a nonzero map `ℱ ⟶ ω_X`, which is injective, so `H⁰(X, ℱ)` embeds into
`H⁰(X, ω_X)`, of dimension `g` by equation [Stacks, Tag 0BY8]. -/
theorem finrank_cohomology_zero_le_of_mono [IsIntegral S.X] {F L : S.X.Modules}
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible S.X.presheaf S.X.ringCatSheaf.2 L] (ι : F ⟶ L) [Mono ι]
    (hFc : F.IsCoherent) (h1 : ¬ IsZero (cohomologyOverField S.k S.f F 1)) :
    FiniteDimensional S.k (cohomologyOverField S.k S.f F 0) ∧
      Module.finrank S.k (cohomologyOverField S.k S.f F 0) ≤ genus S.f := by
  have hdim : topologicalKrullDim S.X ≤ 1 := le_of_eq S.dimension_one
  have hFq : F.IsQuasicoherent := isQuasicoherent_of_isCoherent F
  obtain ⟨φ, hφ⟩ := Stacks.Duality.exists_ne_zero_hom_dualizingSheaf S.f hdim F hFq h1
  have hmono : Mono φ := mono_of_ne_zero_of_mono ι hFc φ hφ
  obtain ⟨-, hinj, -, -, -⟩ := exists_cohomologyOverField_longExactSequence S.k S.f
    (ShortComplex.ShortExact.mk' (ShortComplex.exact_cokernel φ) hmono
      (inferInstance : Epi (cokernel.π φ)))
  have := Stacks.Duality.finiteDimensional_cohomologyOverField_zero_dualizingSheafOverField S.f hdim
  have hfin : FiniteDimensional S.k (cohomologyOverField S.k S.f F 0) :=
    Module.Finite.of_injective (cohomologyOverFieldMap S.k S.f φ 0).hom hinj
  refine ⟨hfin, ?_⟩
  rw [← Stacks.Duality.finrank_cohomologyOverField_zero_dualizingSheafOverField S.f hdim]
  exact LinearMap.finrank_le_finrank_of_injective (f := (cohomologyOverFieldMap S.k S.f φ 0).hom)
    hinj

/-- **An invertible module with a nonzero global section is generated by its global sections at
the generic point**, on an integral `X` in Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B5D]: the cokernel of
`AlgebraicGeometry.globalSectionsHom ℒ` vanishes at the generic point. The stalk of `ℒ` there is
a line over the function field and contains the nonzero germ of the section. -/
theorem genericPoint_notMem_supp_cokernel_globalSectionsHom [IsIntegral S.X] (L : S.X.Modules)
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible S.X.presheaf S.X.ringCatSheaf.2 L] {s : Γ(L, ⊤)} (hs : s ≠ 0) :
    genericPoint S.X ∉ SheafOfModules.supp (cokernel (globalSectionsHom L)) := by
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian S.X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian S.f
  have hev : (globalSectionsHom L).app ⊤
      ((SheafOfModules.freeSection (sectionOfGlobalValue L s)).eval (op ⊤)) = s :=
    (congrArg (fun y : L.sections => y.eval (op ⊤))
      (SheafOfModules.sectionsMap_freeHomEquiv_symm_freeSection _ _)).trans
      (sectionOfGlobalValue_eval_top L s)
  refine genericPoint_notMem_supp_cokernel_of_genericPoint_mem_supp (globalSectionsHom L) (𝟙 L)
    ⟨((globalSectionsFree L).presheaf.Γgerm (genericPoint S.X)).hom
      ((SheafOfModules.freeSection (sectionOfGlobalValue L s)).eval (op ⊤)), ?_⟩
  rw [Category.comp_id]
  refine (congrArg (fun z => z ≠ 0) ((mapFun_Γgerm (globalSectionsHom L) (genericPoint S.X)
    ((SheafOfModules.freeSection (sectionOfGlobalValue L s)).eval (op ⊤))).trans
      (congrArg _ hev))).mpr ?_
  exact Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ReflexiveModules.Γgerm_genericPoint_ne_zero_of_ne_zero L hs

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0E3C.** In Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B5D] assume `X` is integral of genus
`g`, and let `ℒ` be an invertible `𝒪_X`-module. If `deg(ℒ) ≥ 2g`, then `ℒ` is generated by its
global sections. -/
@[stacks 0E3C]
theorem isGeneratedByGlobalSections_of_two_mul_genus_le [IsIntegral S.X] (L : S.X.Modules)
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible S.X.presheaf S.X.ringCatSheaf.2 L]
    (hL : 2 * (genus S.f : ℤ) ≤ invertibleCurveDegree S.k S.f (le_of_eq S.dimension_one) L) :
    SheafOfModules.IsGeneratedByGlobalSections L := by
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian S.X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian S.f
  have : IsNoetherian S.X := isNoetherian_of_locallyOfFiniteType S.f
  have hdim : topologicalKrullDim S.X ≤ 1 := le_of_eq S.dimension_one
  have hLc : L.IsCoherent :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CurveEulerBridge.isCoherent_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank S.k S.f L 1
  have hLq : L.IsQuasicoherent := isQuasicoherent_of_isCoherent L
  have := finiteDimensional_cohomologyOverField_of_isProper S.k S.f L 0
  -- Riemann-Roch: `dim H⁰(X, ℒ) ≥ g + 1`.
  have hRR := finrank_sub_finrank_eq_invertibleCurveDegree_add_genus S.k S.f hdim L
  have hh0 : genus S.f + 1 ≤ Module.finrank S.k (cohomologyOverField S.k S.f L 0) := by
    have : (0 : ℤ) ≤ Module.finrank S.k (cohomologyOverField S.k S.f L 1) := Int.natCast_nonneg _
    omega
  -- a nonzero global section
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ : ∃ s : Γ(L, ⊤), s ≠ 0 := by
    by_contra hcon
    push Not at hcon
    have : Subsingleton (cohomologyOverField S.k S.f L 0) :=
      (cohomologyOverFieldZeroEquivSections S.k S.f L).subsingleton_congr.mpr
        ⟨fun a b => (hcon a).trans (hcon b).symm⟩
    rw [Module.finrank_zero_of_subsingleton] at hh0
    omega
  -- the quotient `𝒬` of `ℒ` by the submodule generated by the global sections
  set γ := globalSectionsHom L
  set π := cokernel.π γ
  refine nonempty_generatingSections_of_epi_globalSectionsHom L (epi_of_isZero_cokernel γ ?_)
  by_contra hQ
  have hQc : (cokernel γ).IsCoherent :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentOfFiniteType.isCoherent_of_epi_of_isQuasicoherent hLc π
  have hQdim : topologicalKrullDim (SheafOfModules.supp (cokernel γ)) ≤ 0 :=
    topologicalKrullDim_supp_le_zero_of_genericPoint_notMem hdim _
      (@_root_.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent.isFiniteType _ _ _ _ hQc)
      (genericPoint_notMem_supp_cokernel_globalSectionsHom L hs)
  have hQ0 : ¬ IsZero (cohomologyOverField S.k S.f (cokernel γ) 0) := fun h =>
    hQ (S.isZero_of_supp_dim_le_zero_of_isZero_sections hQc hQdim h)
  -- the long exact sequence of `0 ⟶ ℒ' ⟶ ℒ ⟶ 𝒬 ⟶ 0`
  have hT := ShortComplex.shortExact_mk_kernel_ι π
  obtain ⟨d, -, hfg, hgd, -⟩ := exists_cohomologyOverField_longExactSequence S.k S.f hT
  have hzero : ∀ a, cohomologyOverFieldMap S.k S.f π 0 a = 0 := fun a =>
    cohomologyOverFieldMap_zero_eq_zero_of_globalSectionsHom_comp S.f π (cokernel.condition γ) a
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (cohomologyOverFieldMap S.k S.f (kernel.ι π) 0) :=
    fun b => (hfg 0 b).mp (hzero b)
  have h1 : ¬ IsZero (cohomologyOverField S.k S.f (kernel π) 1) := by
    intro h
    refine hQ0 (@ModuleCat.isZero_of_subsingleton _ _ _ ⟨fun a b => ?_⟩)
    have hd : ∀ c, d 0 c = 0 := fun c => h.eq_of_tgt (d 0) 0 ▸ rfl
    obtain ⟨a', ha'⟩ := (hgd 0 a).mp (hd a)
    obtain ⟨b', hb'⟩ := (hgd 0 b).mp (hd b)
    rw [← ha', ← hb', hzero, hzero]
  have hL'c : (kernel π).IsCoherent :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentOfFiniteType.isCoherent_of_mono_of_isQuasicoherent hLc
      (kernel.ι π)
  obtain ⟨hfin, hle⟩ := finrank_cohomology_zero_le_of_mono (kernel.ι π) hL'c h1
  have := LinearMap.finrank_le_finrank_of_surjective
    (f := (cohomologyOverFieldMap S.k S.f (kernel.ι π) 0).hom) hsurj
  omega

/-! ### Restriction to a closed subscheme -/

/-- **The restriction `ℒ|_Z` of a module to a closed subscheme `Z`, as an `𝒪_X`-module**: the
tensor product `ℒ ⊗_{𝒪_X} i_* 𝒪_Z`, where `i : Z ⟶ X` is the inclusion. Its global sections are
the space `H⁰(X, ℒ|_Z)` of [Stacks, Tag 0E3D]. -/
abbrev subschemeRestriction (L : S.X.Modules) (Z : S.X.IdealSheafData) : S.X.Modules :=
  (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u}
      ⟨S.X.presheaf, Presheaf.isSheaf_of_isSheaf_comp _ S.X.presheaf
        (forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat) S.X.ringCatSheaf.2⟩).obj L)).obj
    ((RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction.modulePushforward Z.subschemeι.toLRSHom.toShHom).obj
      (SheafOfModules.unit (structureSheafRing Z.subscheme.toRingedSpace)))

/-- `ℒ ⊗ 𝒪_X`, the middle term of the ideal sequence of `Z` tensored with `ℒ`. -/
abbrev tensorStructureSheaf (L : S.X.Modules) : S.X.Modules :=
  (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u}
      ⟨S.X.presheaf, Presheaf.isSheaf_of_isSheaf_comp _ S.X.presheaf
        (forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat) S.X.ringCatSheaf.2⟩).obj L)).obj
    (SheafOfModules.unit (structureSheafRing S.X.toRingedSpace))

/-- The right unitor `ℒ ⊗ 𝒪_X ≅ ℒ`, as an isomorphism of `𝒪_X`-modules. -/
def tensorStructureSheafIso (L : S.X.Modules) : S.tensorStructureSheaf L ≅ L :=
  SheafOfModules.tensorSheafUnitRightIso S.X.toRingedSpace L

/-- `ℐ_Z ℒ ⟶ ℒ ⊗ 𝒪_X`: the inclusion `ℐ_Z ⟶ 𝒪_X` tensored with `ℒ`. -/
def tensorDivisorIdealMap (Z : S.X.IdealSheafData) (L : S.X.Modules) :
    S.idealTwist Z L ⟶ S.tensorStructureSheaf L :=
  (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u}
      ⟨S.X.presheaf, Presheaf.isSheaf_of_isSheaf_comp _ S.X.presheaf
        (forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat) S.X.ringCatSheaf.2⟩).obj L)).map
    (Stacks.IdealSheafSequence.divisorIdealMap Z)

/-- `ℒ ⊗ 𝒪_X ⟶ ℒ|_Z`: the restriction of functions `𝒪_X ⟶ i_* 𝒪_Z` tensored with `ℒ`. -/
def tensorDivisorQuotientMap (Z : S.X.IdealSheafData) (L : S.X.Modules) :
    S.tensorStructureSheaf L ⟶ S.subschemeRestriction L Z :=
  (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u}
      ⟨S.X.presheaf, Presheaf.isSheaf_of_isSheaf_comp _ S.X.presheaf
        (forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat) S.X.ringCatSheaf.2⟩).obj L)).map
    (Stacks.IdealSheafSequence.divisorQuotientMap Z)

/-- **The restriction map `ℒ ⟶ ℒ|_Z`**: `ℒ ≅ ℒ ⊗ 𝒪_X ⟶ ℒ ⊗ i_* 𝒪_Z`, induced by the restriction
of functions `𝒪_X ⟶ i_* 𝒪_Z`. -/
def subschemeRestrictionπ (Z : S.X.IdealSheafData) (L : S.X.Modules) :
    L ⟶ S.subschemeRestriction L Z :=
  (S.tensorStructureSheafIso L).inv ≫ S.tensorDivisorQuotientMap Z L

/-- `ℐ_Z ℒ ⟶ ℒ` is `ℒ ⊗ ℐ_Z ⟶ ℒ ⊗ 𝒪_X` followed by the right unitor. -/
theorem idealTwistι_eq (Z : S.X.IdealSheafData) (L : S.X.Modules) :
    S.idealTwistι Z L = S.tensorDivisorIdealMap Z L ≫ (S.tensorStructureSheafIso L).hom :=
  rfl

/-- **The ideal sequence of `Z` tensored with an invertible `ℒ` is short exact**:
`0 ⟶ ℒ ⊗ ℐ_Z ⟶ ℒ ⊗ 𝒪_X ⟶ ℒ ⊗ i_* 𝒪_Z ⟶ 0`. The ideal sequence is [Stacks, Tag 0C6K], and tensoring
with an invertible module is an equivalence of categories, hence exact. -/
theorem exists_shortExact_tensorDivisor (Z : S.X.IdealSheafData) (L : S.X.Modules)
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible S.X.presheaf S.X.ringCatSheaf.2 L] :
    ∃ hz : S.tensorDivisorIdealMap Z L ≫ S.tensorDivisorQuotientMap Z L = 0,
      (ShortComplex.mk _ _ hz).ShortExact := by
  let F : S.X.Modules ⥤ S.X.Modules := (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u}
    ⟨S.X.presheaf, Presheaf.isSheaf_of_isSheaf_comp _ S.X.presheaf
      (forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat) S.X.ringCatSheaf.2⟩).obj L
  have : F.IsEquivalence :=
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isInvertible_iff_tensorLeftFunctor_isEquivalence _ _ L).mp ‹_›
  have h0 : F.PreservesZeroMorphisms := Functor.preservesZeroMorphisms_of_isLeftAdjoint _
  obtain ⟨hz, hT⟩ := Stacks.IdealSheafSequence.divisorIdeal_shortExact Z
  let E := F.asEquivalence
  exact ⟨(F.map_comp _ _).symm.trans ((congrArg F.map hz).trans
      (@Functor.map_zero _ _ _ _ _ _ _ h0 _ _)),
    @ShortComplex.ShortExact.map _ _ _ _ _ _ _ hT F h0
      (inferInstance : E.functor.PreservesLeftHomologyOf _)
      (inferInstance : E.functor.PreservesRightHomologyOf _)
      (@Functor.map_mono _ _ _ _ _
        (@Functor.preservesMonomorphisms_of_isRightAdjoint _ _ _ _ _
          E.symm.toAdjunction.isRightAdjoint) _ _ _ hT.mono_f)
      (@Functor.map_epi _ _ _ _ _
        (@Functor.preservesEpimorphisms_of_isLeftAdjoint _ _ _ _ _ E.toAdjunction.isLeftAdjoint)
        _ _ _ hT.epi_g)⟩

/-- `ℐ_Z ℒ ⟶ ℒ ⟶ ℒ|_Z` is zero. -/
theorem idealTwistι_comp_subschemeRestrictionπ (Z : S.X.IdealSheafData) (L : S.X.Modules)
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible S.X.presheaf S.X.ringCatSheaf.2 L] :
    S.idealTwistι Z L ≫ S.subschemeRestrictionπ Z L = 0 := by
  rw [idealTwistι_eq, subschemeRestrictionπ, Category.assoc, Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc]
  exact (S.exists_shortExact_tensorDivisor Z L).1

/-- **The sequence `0 ⟶ ℐ_Z ℒ ⟶ ℒ ⟶ ℒ|_Z ⟶ 0` is short exact** for an invertible `ℒ`: it is the
ideal sequence `0 ⟶ ℐ_Z ⟶ 𝒪_X ⟶ i_* 𝒪_Z ⟶ 0` of [Stacks, Tag 0C6K] tensored with `ℒ`, followed
by the right unitor `ℒ ⊗ 𝒪_X ≅ ℒ`. -/
theorem shortExact_idealTwistι_subschemeRestrictionπ (Z : S.X.IdealSheafData) (L : S.X.Modules)
    [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible S.X.presheaf S.X.ringCatSheaf.2 L] :
    (ShortComplex.mk (S.idealTwistι Z L) (S.subschemeRestrictionπ Z L)
      (S.idealTwistι_comp_subschemeRestrictionπ Z L)).ShortExact := by
  obtain ⟨hz, hT⟩ := S.exists_shortExact_tensorDivisor Z L
  refine ShortComplex.shortExact_of_iso ?_ hT
  refine ShortComplex.isoMk (Iso.refl _) (S.tensorStructureSheafIso L) (Iso.refl _) ?_ ?_
  · exact (Category.id_comp _).trans (S.idealTwistι_eq Z L)
  · exact (Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc (S.tensorStructureSheafIso L) _).trans (Category.comp_id _).symm

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0E3D.** In Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B5D] assume `X` is integral of genus
`g`, let `ℒ` be an invertible `𝒪_X`-module, and let `Z ⊆ X` be a nonempty `0`-dimensional closed
subscheme. If `deg(ℒ) ≥ 2g - 1 + deg(Z)`, then `ℒ` is generated by its global sections and
`H⁰(X, ℒ) ⟶ H⁰(X, ℒ|_Z)` is surjective.

Here `deg(Z) = dim_k Γ(Z, 𝒪_Z)` and `ℒ|_Z = ℒ ⊗ i_* 𝒪_Z`. Global generation is [Stacks, Tag 0E3C],
as `deg(Z) ≥ 1`; the surjectivity follows from `H¹(X, ℐ_Z ℒ) = 0`, which is [Stacks, Tag 0E3A]
since `deg(ℒ) > 2g - 2 + deg(Z)`. -/
@[stacks 0E3D]
theorem isGeneratedByGlobalSections_and_surjective_subschemeRestrictionπ [IsIntegral S.X]
    (L : S.X.Modules) [SheafOfModules.IsInvertible S.X.presheaf S.X.ringCatSheaf.2 L]
    (Z : S.X.IdealSheafData) (hZ : topologicalKrullDim Z.subscheme ≤ 0)
    (hZne : Nonempty Z.subscheme)
    (hL : 2 * (genus S.f : ℤ) - 1 + (S.subschemeDegree Z : ℤ) ≤
      invertibleCurveDegree S.k S.f (le_of_eq S.dimension_one) L) :
    SheafOfModules.IsGeneratedByGlobalSections L ∧
      Function.Surjective (cohomologyOverFieldMap S.k S.f (S.subschemeRestrictionπ Z L) 0) := by
  have hdeg : 1 ≤ S.subschemeDegree Z := by
    let : Algebra S.k Γ(Z.subscheme, ⊤) :=
      ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of S.k)).inv ≫ (Z.subschemeι ≫ S.f).appTop).hom.toAlgebra
    have := S.finiteDimensional_globalSections_subscheme Z
    have := Stacks.EmptyLimitCounterexample.nontrivial_Γ_of_nonempty Z.subscheme hZne.some
    exact Module.finrank_pos
